# Vercel deploy bundle control.
#
# `vercel --prod` (CLI) bundles the whole WORKING DIRECTORY, not just git-tracked
# files — so it picks up local caches written by another user (the cross-session
# ownership scheme) and fails with EACCES, and would otherwise upload secrets and
# multi-MB local artifacts. The GitHub-integration build only sees git-tracked
# files so it never hit these. This list makes both paths bundle the same minimal
# set: the function needs only api/, public/, requirements.txt, vercel.json, and
# scripts/tutor.py (imported by api/_openbrain_api.py at runtime).

# ── Caches / build cruft (cross-owned -> EACCES, and pure bloat) ──
.git
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache

# ── Secrets — never upload local env files (Vercel uses dashboard env vars) ──
.env
.env.*

# ── Broken local symlink (iCloud Obsidian vault) — absent in the build env ──
vault

# ── Large local artifacts not used by the API ──
brain_index/
test-fixtures/
backups/
ingest/
upload_target/

# ── Local-only tooling / standalone servers (KEEP scripts/tutor.py) ──
scripts/*
!scripts/tutor.py
brain_server/
mcp_server/
/app.py          # root dev entrypoint ONLY — leading slash so it does NOT also match api/app.py
config/

# ── Migrations, tests, docs — not needed at runtime ──
supabase/
tests/
docs/

# ── Dev / meta ──
Makefile
pyrightconfig.json
requirements-dev.txt
requirements-full.txt
*.md
